# Go
/bin/
/out/
# `/api` used to be here, for a binary dropped by a bare `go build -o api`. It
# also matched the api/ directory — a gitignore pattern cannot tell the two
# apart — so the OpenAPI contract and its tests were silently untracked.
#
# Now that api/ exists, `go build -o api` writes *into* it instead, so the
# 28 MB binary lands next to the contract. That specific path is what needs
# ignoring; the directory itself must stay tracked.
/api/api
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Env / secrets
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
pipelines/.venv/

# pipelines/uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, and that was wrong on
# two counts: every build resolved dependencies afresh, so "runs reproducibly
# anywhere" (E4-S1) was not true — and Dockerfile.ingest copies the lockfile to
# install with `uv sync --locked`, which fails on a clean checkout when the file
# is not in the repository. Verified: the ingestion image would not build in CI.

# Pipeline data (raw downloads & generated outputs; overrides ARE tracked)
#
# Everything downloaded from a source stays out of git, whatever its extension.
# The previous `*.pdf` rule only covered the GKV list, so a 5.4 MB
# Bundes-Klinik-Atlas export sat here untracked but not ignored — one `git add -A`
# from entering the history of a repository that is heading for public. Raw
# downloads also age; a file in git is a snapshot nobody re-fetches.
pipelines/data/raw/*
!pipelines/data/raw/.gitkeep
pipelines/data/processed/

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/

# pip-audit export (CI artifact)
pipelines/requirements-audit.txt
dist/
